WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.082
Because of the lagoon adventure, the Indians became Peter's friends.

2
00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:08.022
Peter had saved Tiger Lily's life.

3
00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:14.128
Now she and her tribe kept faithful watch over the Lost Boys' underground home.

4
00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:17.951
Night and day, they guarded Peter and his family.

5
00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:24.035
They called Peter "The Great White Father," which he quite liked.

6
00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:32.295
He would say to them, "The Great White Father is glad to see the warriors protecting his home from the pirates."

7
00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:36.601
But Tiger Lily did not want Wendy to be called Peter's wife.

8
00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:41.193
The Indian princess had become quite fond of the little boy as well.

9
00:00:41.194 --> 00:00:45.869
And, like Tinker Bell, she was jealous of Wendy.

10
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:52.851
One evening, the Indians were at their watch as usual while the children were having dinner below.

11
00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:56.829
Peter wasn't home because he had gone to find out the time.

12
00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:01.579
On the island, one found out the time by finding the crocodile.

13
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:07.716
When the clock inside the crocodile struck the hour, one knew what time it was.

14
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:13.180
The meal was make-believe, and the boys were particularly noisy and difficult.

15
00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:16.005
Wendy asked for silence.

16
00:01:16.006 --> 00:01:22.619
"If you have any complaints," she said, "you must first raise your hands to speak."

17
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.322
All their hands went up at once.

18
00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:28.690
"Slightly is eating all the food!"

19
00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:32.185
"Nibs is sneezing on the table!"

20
00:01:32.186 --> 00:01:34.452
"The twins took too much dessert!"

21
00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:38.817
"Curly isn't using his knife and fork!"

22
00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:42.298
After the meal, things quieted down.

23
00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:46.046
They all helped clean the table and put the door away.

24
00:01:46.047 --> 00:01:50.913
Wendy went back to her sewing while the boys danced and played by the fire.

25
00:01:50.914 --> 00:01:56.492
It was a familiar scene in their home, perhaps for the last time.

26
00:01:56.493 --> 00:02:00.251
Suddenly they could hear footsteps above them.

27
00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:04.952
"Children, that must be your father," said Wendy.

28
00:02:04.953 --> 00:02:07.841
"He likes it when you greet him."

29
00:02:07.842 --> 00:02:11.842
Outside, Peter was saying good night to the Indians.

30
00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:18.120
"Keep a safe watch over us tonight!" he said, before slipping into his tree.

31
00:02:18.121 --> 00:02:25.011
When he opened the round door underground, the children joyfully dragged him from his tunnel.

32
00:02:25.012 --> 00:02:29.807
Peter had brought nuts for the boys and the time of day for Wendy.

33
00:02:29.808 --> 00:02:34.974
"Peter, you will spoil them, you know," Wendy said.

34
00:02:34.975 --> 00:02:41.524
"Father," said Curly, "we're dancing and we want you to dance with us."

35
00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:47.602
Peter liked dancing, but for fun he pretended to be a tired father coming home from work.

36
00:02:47.603 --> 00:02:54.092
"Me?" he groaned. "My old bones can hardly walk!"

37
00:02:54.093 --> 00:02:58.676
"And we want Mother to dance too," said Slightly.

38
00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:02.939
"What?" cried Wendy, joining the game.

39
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:08.182
"This old mother of so many boys has lots to do!"

40
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:12.550
"But it's Saturday night!" shouted Michael.

41
00:03:12.551 --> 00:03:17.337
However, no one knew if it was really Saturday night.

42
00:03:17.338 --> 00:03:21.296
They had lost count of the days of the week long ago.

43
00:03:21.297 --> 00:03:30.094
When they wanted to have a special evening, they always called it "Saturday night."

44
00:03:30.095 --> 00:03:37.701
Peter and Wendy promised to dance with them, but first the boys would have to put on their pajamas and get ready for bed.

45
00:03:37.702 --> 00:03:42.373
While they waited for the boys, Peter joined Wendy at the fire.

46
00:03:42.374 --> 00:03:45.337
She looked at him lovingly.

47
00:03:45.338 --> 00:03:50.538
"They are sweet, our little family, don't you think?" said Wendy.

48
00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:54.828
Peter suddenly looked troubled. "What is it, Peter?"

49
00:03:54.829 --> 00:04:03.100
"It's only make-believe that I am their father, right?" replied Peter in a shaky voice.

50
00:04:03.101 --> 00:04:06.240
"Oh, yes," said Wendy.

51
00:04:06.241 --> 00:04:12.900
"You see," he continued, "it would make me old to be their real father."

52
00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:20.244
"Peter, after all this time together, what do I mean to you?" asked Wendy.

53
00:04:20.245 --> 00:04:23.607
His answer was not what she had hoped for.

54
00:04:23.608 --> 00:04:28.342
"I am your devoted son," replied Peter.

55
00:04:28.343 --> 00:04:34.690
"I understand," she said, but it really was very confusing.

56
00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:39.479
Wendy got up from her seat and went to another corner of the room.

57
00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.824
"Sometimes you are very strange," Peter said to her.

58
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:51.464
"And so is Tiger Lily. She says she wants to mean something to me, but doesn't want to be my mother."

59
00:04:51.465 --> 00:04:59.650
"Perhaps Tinker Bell can explain it to you," Wendy answered, frowning.

